class:: SpecPcile2
summary:: Generalized spectral percentile frequency
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/SpecPcile

description::
Finds the frequency below which the requested fraction of selected spectral weight lies. Optional within-bin interpolation avoids quantizing every answer to a bin center. Silence returns zero.

This is a non-destructive FFT reader. It is practically similar to link::Classes/SpecPcile:: and conventional spectral rolloff, but exposes the cumulative fraction, magnitude/power convention, bounds, interpolation, and units directly.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: chain
An FFT chain matching code::fftSize::.

argument:: fraction
Cumulative fraction from 0 through 1; 0.85 is a common rolloff value.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included frequency in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included frequency in Hz; 0 selects Nyquist.

argument:: interpolate
Nonzero enables linear location within the crossing bin.

argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 uses magnitude and 1 uses power.

argument:: fftSize
Literal FFT size from 256 through 8192.

returns::
Percentile frequency in Hz.

instancemethods::

examples::
The 85-percent rolloff follows spectral brightness and controls the cutoff of the audible source.
code::
(
Routine({
    ~mir2Buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var value = SpecPcile2.kr(chain, 0.85, fftSize: 1024);
        LPF.ar(source, value.clip(150, 9000).lag(0.05)) * 0.3 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.3) ! 2
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
~mir2Buffer.free;
)
::

